# With `bun checkfu deploy`, a variable exported in your shell, or set in a file
# Bun loads on its own such as .env.local, is used for any entry left empty
# here, and an entry with a value here wins over both. CHECKFU_JURISDICTION is
# fixed to what the deploy checked, so neither can change it. The
# exception is CHECKFU_API_KEY: if both set it to different keys, the deploy
# stops, because later commands would send the shell's key. `bun run dev`,
# `bun run deploy` and `bun run deploy:production` run Alchemy directly, and
# there a value exported in your shell wins over this file.

# Secret clients send in `Authorization: Bearer <key>` or `x-api-key: <key>`.
# Leave it empty and `bun checkfu deploy` generates one, or run: openssl rand -hex 32
CHECKFU_API_KEY=

# Set at least one model provider API key.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Where Durable Objects keep their data. Decide before the first
# deploy: an object inside a jurisdiction is a different object from the one
# with the same name outside it, so changing CHECKFU_JURISDICTION later starts
# from empty. `bun checkfu deploy` records it and refuses a later change unless
# run with --change-jurisdiction. CHECKFU_LOCATION_HINT only affects objects
# created after it is set.
# CHECKFU_JURISDICTION: eu | fedramp | fedramp-high | us
# CHECKFU_LOCATION_HINT: wnam | enam | sam | weur | eeur | apac | apac-ne | apac-se | oc | afr | me
CHECKFU_JURISDICTION=
CHECKFU_LOCATION_HINT=

# Optional. Also serve the API and the MCP server on your own hostnames, for
# example api.example.com and mcp.example.com; the two must differ. Each
# hostname's zone has to be in the Cloudflare account you deploy to; the deploy
# creates the DNS record and certificate and reports these addresses. The
# workers.dev addresses keep working too, with the same API key.
# A hostname set here replaces every custom hostname on that Worker, including
# any attached in the Cloudflare dashboard. Set none to detach them all. Left
# empty here and unset in your shell, hostnames that are already attached stay
# as they are.
# To change a hostname that is already set, set it to none and deploy, then set
# the new one and deploy again. Changing it in one step detaches the old one
# first, so if the new one cannot be attached (a typo, its zone is not in the
# account, or another Worker has it, as in swapping the two) the Worker is left
# with neither.
CHECKFU_API_DOMAIN=
CHECKFU_MCP_DOMAIN=
